{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Break</b> — the tav you will interpret as opposite him: 'HaShem, You were like a man who searches — You would not find the wicked man, for he is lost.'" "And some say: for the tav is a sign of the arm, that You seek the arm [raised] to do evil and do not find it, in the manner of 'You will find Your hand, YHWH.' Then it will be clear that HaShem alone is King, and the witness is: 'the nations perished from His land.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:56.027955433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}